  "correspondence": [
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-1",
      "end_character": 659,
      "excerpt": "A premise is **not** an axiom (`CAV2-D53`): the axiom is held true (high veracity),\nthe premise is a bet (low veracity) even when conviction is high \u2014 `CAV2-D23` keeps\nveracity and commitment separate, and the premise is exactly where they diverge. It\nis **not** an invariant (`CAV2-D54`): the invariant is a must-hold on the system, a\npremise is a proposition to reason from. It is **not** a disposable hypothesis: a\npremise is *load-bearing* (things are built on it) while still unproven \u2014 which is\nwhat makes its defeasibility worth tracking rather than ignoring. Promotion premise\n\u2192 axiom is an evidence-gated lifecycle move (`CAV2-D48`), never automatic.",
      "unit_id": "unit-8dd741b7f25f4f4782dbf67e67db415370ddc1dc77fc8d436dfd9cc6aa79b2d0"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-2",
      "end_character": 177,
      "excerpt": "This target remains distinct from the sibling targets semantic.premise reconstructed from CAV2-D55; shared source lineage does not merge their identities or validation purposes.",
      "unit_id": "unit-f8f3b6bc508b9025b93e6368dab99daa612b71ce809f8e6596f3a495452faadb"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-3",
      "end_character": 251,
      "excerpt": "Candidate Definition reconstructed from an accepted normalization scaffold and exact CyberAlchemy-v2 source sections. It is not admitted and grants no implementation, migration, registry, publication, release, deployment, or external-effect authority.",
      "unit_id": "unit-551051d584e8331e5ddcc495261d314ed89f7cf4cc2e9b5d89d0ceba64f24fbe"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-4",
      "end_character": 411,
      "excerpt": "Use \"premise\" for the load-bearing bets a project stands on *provisionally* \u2014 the\nthings it commits to acting on before they are proven, and expects to test. The\nmarker is a hedge: if a candidate axiom says \"hypothesis\", \"we conjecture \u2014 not\nprove\", or carries `veracidade: low`, it is a premise. A premise earns its way to\naxiom only through the evidence/promotion path (`CAV2-D48`), never by conviction\nalone.",
      "unit_id": "unit-511822bee042c6819bb8deeadbf1e756cc5249a31633a11c187285c4ff913b0c"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-5",
      "end_character": 22,
      "excerpt": "scope.shared-authority",
      "unit_id": "unit-d98b0dcc8c90b5d742e9beb805c5005c88770dc54b7c3939d5b7cc2388378d48"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-6",
      "end_character": 78,
      "excerpt": "Admission, activation, publication, release, deployment, and external effects.",
      "unit_id": "unit-8dec732fb5d927545d4bf5c1bea73405d34e388983cdba3240a36b63ba348803"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-7",
      "end_character": 88,
      "excerpt": "Meanings assigned to split or reclassified sibling targets unless explicitly referenced.",
      "unit_id": "unit-94bf2030418c421474ce1629a5f3255fde290758d03623f29467345f93ee9ea0"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-8",
      "end_character": 83,
      "excerpt": "Resolve semantic.hypothesis by its machine identity rather than its directory name.",
      "unit_id": "unit-dc3131809466ac498245a6d685763fa0929f3f85b8c6b345fd2d12e2dd834454"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-9",
      "end_character": 79,
      "excerpt": "Challenge source drift through the L1 drift audit before relying on Hypothesis.",
      "unit_id": "unit-55709ef9230cc939664eae44c89722581ddcdbcf72afe76fdae93ae7665e86e7"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-10",
      "end_character": 772,
      "excerpt": "In CyberAlchemy-lab migration work, Hypothesis is a prototype meaning reconstructed from CAL-NORMALIZE-01. It remains non-authoritative until the correct Lab owner admits a fully validated candidate.\n\nSource context retained for reconstruction:\n\nIn the vault corpora, premises live beside axioms (`business-premises`,\n`ontology-premises`, `system-premises`) and \"sit on top of\" them; `veracidade: low\n/ convic\u00e7\u00e3o: high` is the premise signature. ZefraHub `AX-ONT-7` (\"we conjecture \u2014\nnot prove\") and `AX-SYS-3` (\"the folder structure is a hypothesis\") are premises\nmislabeled as axioms. Demotion is normal and healthy: a vault moved an\n\"adaptive-system axiom\" to the `P-ONT-9` premise because it was \"an engineering\ncommitment about maintenance, not a foundational truth.\"",
      "unit_id": "unit-d07b76e447203e95001dbc6fb32ea044fd1d69fb078b6480cc8e8440ac923c34"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-11",
      "end_character": 41,
      "excerpt": "/home/vrondelli/projects/CyberAlchemy-lab",
      "unit_id": "unit-ffa309e64b53ab85866dd9c0bce78b5cb2d9a40913e906c9ea92bc3faa5b2ed5"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-12",
      "end_character": 116,
      "excerpt": "A hypothesis is an idea framed so evidence can test it, not an assumption the project has already chosen to rely on.",
      "unit_id": "unit-6865c193772552a0d17911ff5b7bbf1295e5561a775e1f27ead3c7b4d7e35923"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-13",
      "end_character": 659,
      "excerpt": "A premise is **not** an axiom (`CAV2-D53`): the axiom is held true (high veracity),\nthe premise is a bet (low veracity) even when conviction is high \u2014 `CAV2-D23` keeps\nveracity and commitment separate, and the premise is exactly where they diverge. It\nis **not** an invariant (`CAV2-D54`): the invariant is a must-hold on the system, a\npremise is a proposition to reason from. It is **not** a disposable hypothesis: a\npremise is *load-bearing* (things are built on it) while still unproven \u2014 which is\nwhat makes its defeasibility worth tracking rather than ignoring. Promotion premise\n\u2192 axiom is an evidence-gated lifecycle move (`CAV2-D48`), never automatic.",
      "unit_id": "unit-e5ce6f94187cc4d4a12b6d64b3d84910cc42b961c7233263b4f3e1afc630c384"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-14",
      "end_character": 177,
      "excerpt": "This target remains distinct from the sibling targets semantic.premise reconstructed from CAV2-D55; shared source lineage does not merge their identities or validation purposes.",
      "unit_id": "unit-c1d24f90e102d2d392b58d5f2a420248f35e32efbcbf8c6baad0c0cacf338f7c"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-15",
      "end_character": 621,
      "excerpt": "```text\npremise P:  adopted-to-proceed(P) \u2227 \u00acestablished-true(P) \u2227 defeasible(P)\n            typically veracity(P) = low, conviction(P) = high   (CAV2-D23: the two axes diverge)\nlifecycle:  P --evidence--> { promote \u2192 axiom (CAV2-D48) | revise | retire }\ndistinguished-from:\n  axiom (CAV2-D53):      veracity high, held true     \u2192 a premise is a bet\n  invariant (CAV2-D54):  a must-hold on the system    \u2192 a premise is a proposition to reason from\n```\n\nThe premise is exactly the case where **veracity and conviction diverge**\n(`CAV2-D23`): the project may be highly committed to acting on `P` while `P`\nremains unproven.",
      "unit_id": "unit-ecde379b668101ac4ba4a26b9ff914246c56019c7dc5075d08eacc176b894484"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-16",
      "end_character": 1192,
      "excerpt": "Hypothesis is the normalized definition identified by semantic.hypothesis, owned within scope.shared-authority, and carried by type.definition. Any canonical instance must preserve that classification and the accepted source relations to CAV2-D55 without silently merging it with another target.\n\nTarget-specific normative meaning:\n\nA Hypothesis is a falsifiable provisional proposition posed for investigation or experiment, with declared observations or outcomes that could support, refine, or reject it; it is not adopted as a working basis merely by being stated.\n\nBound source-semantic basis:\n\nA premise is a **working proposition the project adopts in order to proceed\nwithout having established it as true** \u2014 a defeasible bet or commitment,\ncharacteristically held at **low veracity but often high conviction**\n(`veracidade: low`, `convic\u00e7\u00e3o: high`) \u2014 that is expected to be revised, promoted,\nor retired as evidence accumulates. A premise may complement axioms (a working\nelaboration built on the bedrock) or stand alone as a conjecture the project is\nbetting on. It can provisionally ground invariants and rules, but it does **not**\ncarry the settled truth of an axiom (`CAV2-D53`).",
      "unit_id": "unit-24b4b0dba500a900ddcc3fcfb2f89cef49020e73c4879aac86fb38182c329871"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-17",
      "end_character": 42,
      "excerpt": "Stable normalized identity for Hypothesis.",
      "unit_id": "unit-e7ed8e2f77ca15b3c5bc122ae11d18ffec1d8c9138e36fc450e458f944b9ea80"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-18",
      "end_character": 19,
      "excerpt": "semantic.hypothesis",
      "unit_id": "unit-0b752071b61c6ee93892fb94abfd8e3ecfa1998a7b617bc9624149fdf3a68e1a"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-19",
      "end_character": 49,
      "excerpt": "Bound CyberAlchemy-v2 source-definition identity.",
      "unit_id": "unit-589257840cd95cd1a238672e86bd6b9137eba67d8ce5929322ef98c2127693fd"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-20",
      "end_character": 8,
      "excerpt": "CAV2-D55",
      "unit_id": "unit-e2dc872fe0cab23269424c97b886609646134f88f82910e0dc4c831e53bd56b0"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-21",
      "end_character": 57,
      "excerpt": "The candidate identity remains cal.definition.hypothesis.",
      "unit_id": "unit-5f8934298727b6f4fe55b6e153edede0bb8dfb36ae6b1ab9b459e9dcf251b316"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-22",
      "end_character": 53,
      "excerpt": "Every selected source-section digest remains current.",
      "unit_id": "unit-62d9b9f0f2e14b44077e3a0db7904079fca058376b549a92223861c2220f97bc"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-23",
      "end_character": 51,
      "excerpt": "The machine record validates against Definition/v1.",
      "unit_id": "unit-6e0a36a3e7ce10e3274f2fe9e2ee41f7701f2c203d126d1278b94a5f3bd6b8fd"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-24",
      "end_character": 68,
      "excerpt": "The human projection is regenerated exactly from the machine record.",
      "unit_id": "unit-6e3477ec8786dca6eee728124933d1959d2501d9fa6c5a4a317baaec6d87d593"
    }
  ],
